# zensim-fork Phase 4 20-cell smoke bench
# Generated: 2026-05-25
# Source example: jxl-encoder/examples/zensim_loop_smoke_bench.rs
# Mirrors: cvvdp-fork Phase 4 cvvdp_loop_smoke_bench (cell shape + cell selection identical)

## Methodology

For each of 5 synthetic fixtures × 4 distances {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0}:
- Encode with `LossyConfig::new(d).with_strategy(Zenjxl).with_effort(8).with_perceptual_metric(Butteraugli)` (default) → `backend = B`
- Encode with `with_perceptual_metric(Zensim).with_perceptual_device(Cpu)` → `backend = Z_CPU`

Effort 8 forces the buttloop to engage (gated at speed_tier <= kKitten in libjxl).
Distances are the same 4 that cvvdp Phase 4 smoke used so the bench shape is
directly comparable across the two fork arcs.

## Fixtures (all synthetic, ≤128×128, no codec-corpus dependency)

- gradient_64 (64×64 RGB linear gradient)
- diagonal_128 (128×128 diagonal stripes + dither)
- noisy_96 (96×96 radial brightness + high-frequency noise)
- flat_grey_32 (32×32 constant gray, all 128)
- checker_64 (64×64 binary 8×8 checker)

## Headline observations (Z_CPU vs B byte delta)

- gradient_64 / diagonal_128 / noisy_96 / checker_64: **Z_CPU produces smaller
  files at every distance** (Δ ranges -10% to -78%).
- flat_grey_32: ±~1-4% (essentially constant byte cost — no signal for either
  metric to converge on; both produce ~93-99 bytes).

The systematic Z_CPU < B byte delta on non-trivial fixtures indicates that the
Phase 4 calibration seed (median over 3 images, with 1.05× tightening) is
**LAX** relative to butteraugli at these distance points. This is expected and
ACCEPTABLE for the Phase 4 baseline — the seed values are honestly derived
from real measurement and the Phase 6 6-backend tracking sweep + Phase 8-zensim
refit (conditional on Pareto < 85%) are queued to refine them against the full
production corpus.

## What this bench deliberately does NOT verify

- That Z_CPU > B byte count (the Phase 4 calibration is intentionally aiming
  for similar achieved zensim quality, not similar bytes).
- Score deltas (NA columns) — Phase 4 scope is structural plumbing + initial
  calibration seed, not score scaffolding.
- Z_GPU backend (gated on `zensim-loop-gpu` + CUDA at runtime, out of Phase 4
  scope).

## Phase 6 follow-on

The full 6-backend tracking sweep (`cvvdp_track_baseline`-style script
extended with `score_zensim_{cpu,gpu}`) is the next chunk. It will:
1. Score every existing tracking-TSV cell with zensim CPU + GPU.
2. Re-rank the Pareto frontier using zensim as the metric.
3. Decide via RFC §5.4 whether to keep the seeded calibration or refit.

## Provenance

- Encoder commit: 956cac4a7860 (zensim-phase4 working copy, on top of Phase 3 7ad7256c)
- jj op: see `jj op log -l 5` in `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--zensim-phase4/`
- Run command:
  ```
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
    --features "__expert butteraugli-loop zensim-loop ssim2-loop parallel" \
    --example zensim_loop_smoke_bench -- \
    --out benchmarks/zensim_loop_smoke_2026-05-25.tsv
  ```
